<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.5.1: Roots of Squares</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02406</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.5.1: Roots of Squares</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d44ae505-1b5f-41cc-8339-9bcec689244b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Here are some squares whose vertices are on a grid.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/700b7d8bfe426c8ce18db3445ff0e69c45963d39"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Find the area and the side length of each square.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="2c72c3d6-9b25-4cb7-ad41-c69f8a623543" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the area of Graph A.</para><para>What is the area of Graph A?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 9 square units.</para><para>The correct answer is 9 square units.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="74826fb0-6fd4-4f69-8928-2f3aa12d03e8" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the side length of Graph A.</para><para>What is the side length of Graph A?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3 units.</para><para>The correct answer is 3 units.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="7a74fc27-e171-4f58-b93c-b6926c75ee18" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the area of Graph B.</para><para>What is the area of Graph B?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 2 square units.</para><para>The correct answer is 2 square units.</para></solution></exercise></section><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is the side length of Graph B?</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\sqrt{2}\) units</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="3367baec-d3e7-4086-beba-94a2e2ba2356" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the area of Graph C.</para><para>What is the area of Graph C?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 10 square units.</para><para>The correct answer is 10 square units.</para></solution></exercise></section><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>What is the side length of Graph C?</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\sqrt{10}\) units</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
</document>
